  'B2',
  '{"passageTitle":"Light Pollution and the Vanishing Night Sky","passageText":"Street lighting makes cities safer and busier, but it also changes the sky. Light that escapes upwards is scattered by dust and water droplets, creating a glow that hides faint stars and disturbs nocturnal animals. Migrating birds can be drawn off course, moths exhaust themselves around lamps, and some trees delay leaf fall near bright streets. The problem is not brightness alone: the direction, colour and timing of light matter. Shields that point light downwards, warmer colours and switches that turn off after midnight reduce the effect at little cost. Dark skies are therefore not a demand to switch everything off, but a request to use light where and when it is actually needed.","gapSentence":{"before":"Street lighting makes cities safer and busier, but it also changes the sky. Light that escapes upwards is ","after":" by dust and water droplets, creating a glow that hides faint stars and disturbs nocturnal animals. Migrating birds can be drawn off course, moths exhaust themselves around lamps, and some trees delay leaf fall near bright streets. The problem is not brightness alone: the direction, colour and timing of light matter. Shields that point light downwards, warmer colours and switches that turn off after midnight reduce the effect at little cost. Dark skies are therefore not a demand to switch everything off, but a request to use light where and when it is actually needed.","correct":"scattered","options":["scattered","absorbed","blocked","cooled"]},"titleQuestion":{"question":"Choose the most appropriate academic title for this passage:","options":["Light Pollution and the Vanishing Night Sky","How Street Lamps Are Manufactured","The Biology of Moths","Why Cities Need Brighter Streets"],"correctIndex":0},"mainIdeaQuestion":{"question":"What is the primary idea of the passage?","options":["Only the brightness of lamps affects the night sky.","Migrating birds are unaffected by artificial light.","Light pollution is about direction, colour and timing as much as brightness.","Cities must remove all street lighting to protect wildlife."],"correctIndex":2},"highlightPrompt":"Highlight the sentence that carries the key claim described in the question.","sentenceOptions":["Light that escapes upwards is scattered by dust and water droplets, creating a glow that hides faint stars and disturbs nocturnal animals.","Leaves also release water vapour, cooling the air around a street by several degrees and lowering the electricity demand of nearby buildings.","During deep sleep, the hippocampus replays sequences of the day in compressed bursts, while the cortex gradually incorporates those patterns into longer-term storage.","Because the receipts were lighter than the coins, they circulated as payment, and the warehouses gradually became banks."]}',
  '{"gapCorrect":"scattered","titleCorrectIndex":0,"mainIdeaCorrectIndex":2,"sentenceCorrectIndex":0,"highlightCorrectSubstring":"Light that escapes upwards is scattered by dust and water droplets, creating a glow that hides faint stars and disturbs nocturnal animals."}',
  120,
