  'C1',
  '{"passageTitle":"The Materials Behind the Pencil","passageText":"The modern pencil began as a lump of graphite wrapped in string. Pure graphite was scarce and soft, so manufacturers ground it, mixed it with clay and fired the mixture into rods. The ratio of clay to graphite determines hardness: more clay gives a faint, durable line for technical drawing, while more graphite gives the dark mark of a sketching pencil. The wooden casing arrived later, partly to stop the graphite from breaking and partly to make an expensive material go further. Pencils therefore record a series of compromises between supply, strength and the darkness of a line. Even a disposable object carries the history of the materials used to make it.","gapSentence":{"before":"The modern pencil began as a lump of ","after":" wrapped in string. Pure graphite was scarce and soft, so manufacturers ground it, mixed it with clay and fired the mixture into rods. The ratio of clay to graphite determines hardness: more clay gives a faint, durable line for technical drawing, while more graphite gives the dark mark of a sketching pencil. The wooden casing arrived later, partly to stop the graphite from breaking and partly to make an expensive material go further. Pencils therefore record a series of compromises between supply, strength and the darkness of a line. Even a disposable object carries the history of the materials used to make it.","correct":"graphite","options":["chalk","wax","ink","graphite"]},"titleQuestion":{"question":"Choose the most appropriate academic title for this passage:","options":["The Invention of Paper","How Erasers Work","A History of Technical Drawing","The Materials Behind the Pencil"],"correctIndex":3},"mainIdeaQuestion":{"question":"What is the primary idea of the passage?","options":["The pencil reflects compromises among scarce materials, strength and line quality.","Pencils are made from a single natural material.","More clay produces a darker pencil line.","Wooden casings were added only for decoration."],"correctIndex":0},"highlightPrompt":"Highlight the sentence that carries the key claim described in the question.","sentenceOptions":["Leaves also release water vapour, cooling the air around a street by several degrees and lowering the electricity demand of nearby buildings.","During deep sleep, the hippocampus replays sequences of the day in compressed bursts, while the cortex gradually incorporates those patterns into longer-term storage.","Because the receipts were lighter than the coins, they circulated as payment, and the warehouses gradually became banks.","The ratio of clay to graphite determines hardness: more clay gives a faint, durable line for technical drawing, while more graphite gives the dark mark of a sketching pencil."]}',
  '{"gapCorrect":"graphite","titleCorrectIndex":3,"mainIdeaCorrectIndex":0,"sentenceCorrectIndex":3,"highlightCorrectSubstring":"The ratio of clay to graphite determines hardness: more clay gives a faint, durable line for technical drawing, while more graphite gives the dark mark of a sketching pencil."}',
