  'B1',
  '{"passageTitle":"Keeping Vaccines Cold from Factory to Clinic","passageText":"A vaccine is only useful if it is still potent when it reaches the patient. Many vaccines must be kept within a narrow temperature range from the factory to the clinic, a system known as the cold chain. The difficulty is not the refrigerator but the gaps between them: a delayed truck, a power cut or a door left open can spoil a whole box. Health programmes therefore use insulated containers, temperature indicators and strict stock rotation. Solar-powered coolers have extended reach in areas without reliable electricity, but they still need maintenance and spare parts. The weakest link is usually the last kilometre, where a clinic may have no trained technician on duty.","gapSentence":{"before":"A vaccine is only useful if it is still ","after":" when it reaches the patient. Many vaccines must be kept within a narrow temperature range from the factory to the clinic, a system known as the cold chain. The difficulty is not the refrigerator but the gaps between them: a delayed truck, a power cut or a door left open can spoil a whole box. Health programmes therefore use insulated containers, temperature indicators and strict stock rotation. Solar-powered coolers have extended reach in areas without reliable electricity, but they still need maintenance and spare parts. The weakest link is usually the last kilometre, where a clinic may have no trained technician on duty.","correct":"potent","options":["affordable","portable","potent","visible"]},"titleQuestion":{"question":"Choose the most appropriate academic title for this passage:","options":["The History of Refrigeration","Why Clinics Need More Doctors","Keeping Vaccines Cold from Factory to Clinic","How Vaccines Are Invented"],"correctIndex":2},"mainIdeaQuestion":{"question":"What is the primary idea of the passage?","options":["Solar coolers remove the need for maintenance.","The factory refrigerator is the weakest part of the system.","Cold-chain failure is most likely in the final stage of delivery.","Vaccines remain effective at any temperature."],"correctIndex":2},"highlightPrompt":"Highlight the sentence that carries the key claim described in the question.","sentenceOptions":["During deep sleep, the hippocampus replays sequences of the day in compressed bursts, while the cortex gradually incorporates those patterns into longer-term storage.","Because the receipts were lighter than the coins, they circulated as payment, and the warehouses gradually became banks.","The difficulty is not the refrigerator but the gaps between them: a delayed truck, a power cut or a door left open can spoil a whole box.","Leaves also release water vapour, cooling the air around a street by several degrees and lowering the electricity demand of nearby buildings."]}',
  '{"gapCorrect":"potent","titleCorrectIndex":2,"mainIdeaCorrectIndex":2,"sentenceCorrectIndex":2,"highlightCorrectSubstring":"The difficulty is not the refrigerator but the gaps between them: a delayed truck, a power cut or a door left open can spoil a whole box."}',
