VALUES (
  'ibir-81',
  'INTERACTIVE_READING',
  'C1',
  '{"passageTitle":"The Air Underground","passageText":"Air quality on underground railways is often worse than on the street above. Trains grind metal wheels against rails, brakes release particles, and the enclosed tunnels trap what is produced. The particles are partly iron-rich dust, which behaves differently from traffic exhaust and may have different health effects. Ventilation helps, but it also pulls in air from the surface, so the benefit depends on the city above. Platform screen doors reduce exposure for waiting passengers, and improved braking materials cut the source. The problem is easy to ignore because the journey is short, but millions of short journeys add up. Monitoring is the first step, since a system that is not measured cannot be improved.","gapSentence":{"before":"Air quality on underground railways is often worse than on the street above. Trains grind metal wheels against rails, brakes release particles, and the ","after":" tunnels trap what is produced. The particles are partly iron-rich dust, which behaves differently from traffic exhaust and may have different health effects. Ventilation helps, but it also pulls in air from the surface, so the benefit depends on the city above. Platform screen doors reduce exposure for waiting passengers, and improved braking materials cut the source. The problem is easy to ignore because the journey is short, but millions of short journeys add up. Monitoring is the first step, since a system that is not measured cannot be improved.","correct":"enclosed","options":["enclosed","raised","lighted","decorated"]},"titleQuestion":{"question":"Choose the most appropriate academic title for this passage:","options":["The Air Underground","The History of the London Tube","How Trains Are Built","Why Cycling Is Dangerous"],"correctIndex":0},"mainIdeaQuestion":{"question":"What is the primary idea of the passage?","options":["Ventilation removes all particles from tunnels.","The health effects of subway dust are fully understood.","Underground air quality is a measurable problem caused by wear and trapped particles.","Subway air is always cleaner than street air."],"correctIndex":2},"highlightPrompt":"Highlight the sentence that carries the key claim described in the question.","sentenceOptions":["Trains grind metal wheels against rails, brakes release particles, and the enclosed tunnels trap what is produced.","Leaves also release water vapour, cooling the air around a street by several degrees and lowering the electricity demand of nearby buildings.","During deep sleep, the hippocampus replays sequences of the day in compressed bursts, while the cortex gradually incorporates those patterns into longer-term storage.","Because the receipts were lighter than the coins, they circulated as payment, and the warehouses gradually became banks."]}',
  '{"gapCorrect":"enclosed","titleCorrectIndex":0,"mainIdeaCorrectIndex":2,"sentenceCorrectIndex":0,"highlightCorrectSubstring":"Trains grind metal wheels against rails, brakes release particles, and the enclosed tunnels trap what is produced."}',
