dardised ingredients ended the need for cookbooks.","Cookbooks became precise as they addressed readers without prior knowledge, encoding social assumptions.","Early cookbooks gave exact quantities for every ingredient."],"correctIndex":2},"highlightPrompt":"Highlight the sentence that carries the key claim described in the question.","sentenceOptions":["During deep sleep, the hippocampus replays sequences of the day in compressed bursts, while the cortex gradually incorporates those patterns into longer-term storage.","Because the receipts were lighter than the coins, they circulated as payment, and the warehouses gradually became banks.","Instructions became more precise when authors began writing for readers who had never seen the dish prepared, and when ingredients became standardized enough to measure.","Leaves also release water vapour, cooling the air around a street by several degrees and lowering the electricity demand of nearby buildings."]}',
