  '{"scenario":"You are meeting your lab partner to resolve a disagreement about data that produced different results.","turns":[{"speaker":"Priya","speakerAudioText":"Your analysis shows a significant effect, but mine does not. Where should we start?","options":["We should report the result that looks better.","One of us must have lied.","Let us delete the whole dataset.","Let us compare the raw files and check whether we cleaned the outliers the same way."],"correctIndex":3},{"speaker":"Priya","speakerAudioText":"I removed three measurements above the detection limit. Did you keep them?","options":["I deleted every value above zero.","I only looked at the graphs.","I kept them and flagged them, because removing them changes the mean substantially.","I did not open the file."],"correctIndex":2},{"speaker":"Priya","speakerAudioText":"So we should report both analyses and explain the difference?","options":["The supervisor does not need to know.","Yes, and we should ask the supervisor which treatment matches the lab protocol.","No, we should hide the disagreement.","We should choose the version that is shorter."],"correctIndex":1}],"summaryPrompt":"Summarise the disagreement, the cause you identified, and the next step with the supervisor."}',
