  '{"scenario":"You are being interviewed by the student newspaper about a proposed tuition increase.","turns":[{"speaker":"Editor Lena","speakerAudioText":"What is your main concern about the increase?","options":["It will hit students who already work part-time and cannot take on more hours.","I think tuition should be higher.","I have no opinion on the proposal.","The newspaper should not cover money."],"correctIndex":0},{"speaker":"Editor Lena","speakerAudioText":"The university says the money is needed for labs. How do you respond?","options":["Labs are irrelevant to education.","The university is always lying.","I refuse to look at any budget.","I would ask for a breakdown of the lab budget before accepting that the increase is unavoidable."],"correctIndex":3},{"speaker":"Editor Lena","speakerAudioText":"Can we quote you by name in the article?","options":["Quote me as the vice-chancellor.","I want to remain anonymous and be named.","Yes, you can use my name and my role as a second-year student.","No, and you cannot use anything I said."],"correctIndex":2}],"summaryPrompt":"Summarise your concern about the fee increase, your response to the university, and the quoting agreement."}',
