  '{"scenario":"You are discussing a peer review you wrote for a student journal with the editor.","turns":[{"speaker":"Dr Lindqvist","speakerAudioText":"Your review says the method is unclear. Can you give the author something specific?","options":["I will repeat that it is unclear.","I will reject the paper without comments.","I will rewrite the paper myself.","I will point to the missing sample size and ask how participants were recruited."],"correctIndex":3},{"speaker":"Dr Lindqvist","speakerAudioText":"The author may disagree. How will you keep the tone constructive?","options":["I will ignore the response.","I will add personal criticism.","I will separate the summary of the paper from the list of requested changes.","I will question the author’s ability."],"correctIndex":2},{"speaker":"Dr Lindqvist","speakerAudioText":"Can you return the revised review by Thursday?","options":["I cannot give a date.","Yes, I will add examples and send it before noon on Thursday.","I need three months.","I have already deleted the draft."],"correctIndex":1}],"summaryPrompt":"Summarise the editor’s feedback, how you will improve the review, and the deadline."}',
